We have opened the doors and our first guest comes in.
He is a man from the neighbourhood.
"Good morning, I would like a cappuccino," he says.
"Gladly, that comes to three Euro fifty," I answer.
Now I step up to the machine.
I am excited because I am making my first coffee today.
But unfortunately I have made a mistake.
The espresso ran much too fast into the cup.
Then I almost dropped the milk jug.
I spilled some milk on the counter.
It is a minor disaster.
Elif sees that immediately and comes over to me.
"No worries, you are still learning to make good espresso," she says kindly.
She remakes the cappuccino for the guest.
The man smiles, takes his coffee and gives us a tip.
"Thank you very much and have a nice weekend," he says.
I take a deep breath.
Hopefully my second coffee will be better!
